<div class="bhd-page__keypoints" aria-label="Active aging hydration principles">
  <div><strong>Risk can rise with age</strong><span>Thirst, kidney function, total body water and access can change over time.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Barriers are often practical</strong><span>Mobility, cognition, swallowing and dependence on others can reduce intake.</span></div>
  <div><strong>More is not always better</strong><span>Heart, kidney and other conditions may require individualized fluid or electrolyte limits.</span></div>
</div>

<section class="bhd-page__feature">
  <div>
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Hydration across later life</p>
    <h2>Older adults are not one group</h2>
    <p>Age-related changes can reduce the margin for fluid imbalance, while medications, illness and practical barriers can add complexity. But a healthy active adult, a frail long-term-care resident and a person with heart or kidney disease may need very different approaches.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section">
  <p class="bhd-page__kicker">What can change</p>
  <h2>Look beyond thirst alone</h2>
  <div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--4">
    <article><h3>Physiology</h3><p>Thirst and kidney water handling can change with age.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Function</h3><p>Mobility, dexterity, vision and cognition can affect access to drinks.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Medications and disease</h3><p>Heart, kidney, endocrine conditions and some medications can change fluid or electrolyte targets.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Environment</h3><p>Heat, exercise, illness and care routines can increase vulnerability.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__prose-grid">
  <article class="bhd-page__prose">
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Where Best Hydrate may fit</p>
    <h2>An option for appropriate adults, not a universal prescription</h2>
    <p>Best Hydrate may suit an older adult who can safely consume the product and prefers a flavoured electrolyte drink during activity, heat or routine use.</p>
    <p>People with prescribed fluid, sodium, potassium or carbohydrate restrictions should follow their healthcare plan.</p>
  </article>
  <aside class="bhd-page__callout">
    <span class="bhd-page__callout-label">Practical support</span>
    <h3>Make safe drinking easier.</h3>
    <p>Visible drinks, preferred cups, regular offers and assistance can matter as much as the beverage itself.</p>
  </aside>
</section>

